###
# Content-Type header of the request to application/json, because Spring needs that header to understand what type of content you are sending in and trigger the appropriate conversion!

POST http://localhost:8081/invoices
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Cache-Control: no-cache

{
  "amount": 5000,
  "user_id": "helene"
}

